# WeChat Mini Program Rules

- Follow the project's existing native Mini Program or framework conventions; do not mix runtimes without an explicit architectural reason.
- Use WXML/WXSS and supported Mini Program APIs rather than assuming browser DOM or unrestricted Node.js capabilities.
- Keep route, component, permission, and subpackage declarations synchronized with `app.json` and page/component JSON files.
- Check platform API availability and runtime compatibility in the relevant Developer Tools configuration before relying on an API.
- Keep secrets out of client-side code and handle permission denial, network failures, and asynchronous errors.
- For AI mode skill generation, validation, or evaluation, use the corresponding `ai-mode-skills` repository skill and follow its own instructions.
